      "side": 1,
      "message": "This makes it so we always see `MODE_DP_PIN_D`. Isn\u0027t it better to call `pd_dfp_dp_get_pin_mode()` and then force `MODE_DP_PIN_C` to `MODE_DP_PIN_D`? If I do that then when I have a charger connected it doesn\u0027t says DP mode is D in the `ectool typecstatus`. If I just use this CL it shows the DP mode there. I think we should return 0 from here when DP mode is not in use.\n\n```\ndiff --git a/baseboard/trogdor/usb_pd_policy.c b/baseboard/trogdor/usb_pd_policy.c\nindex 3b072ed8ba51..e4d15ebe630e 100644\n--- a/baseboard/trogdor/usb_pd_policy.c\n+++ b/baseboard/trogdor/usb_pd_policy.c\n@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@\n #include \"gpio.h\"\n #include \"system.h\"\n #include \"usb_mux.h\"\n+#include \"usb_pd.h\"\n #include \"usbc_ppc.h\"\n #include \"util.h\"\n \n@@ -91,8 +92,13 @@ int pd_snk_is_vbus_provided(int port)\n #ifdef CONFIG_USB_PD_ALT_MODE_DFP\n __override uint8_t get_dp_pin_mode(int port)\n {\n+       int mode \u003d pd_dfp_dp_get_pin_mode(port, dp_status[port]);\n+\n        /* Only support pin assignment D as 2 lanes are reserved to USB SS. */\n-       return MODE_DP_PIN_D;\n+       if (mode \u003d\u003d MODE_DP_PIN_C)\n+               return MODE_DP_PIN_D;\n+\n+       return mode;\n }\n \n __override int svdm_dp_config(int port, uint32_t *payload)\n```",
